<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-coprinopsis-cinerea-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Coprinopsis cinerea Schnakenberg wavelength selection at 77 µm (Pass 1) (Coprinopsis cinerea)",
        "Coprinopsis cinerea Schnakenberg wavelength selection at 77 µm (Pass 1) faithfully reproduces Coprinopsis cinerea morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coprinopsis-cinerea-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coprinopsis-cinerea-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-coprinopsis-cinerea-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-coprinopsis-cinerea-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Coprinopsis cinerea specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-coprinopsis-cinerea-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Coprinopsis cinerea" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A predecessor or successor chronospecies (this series is 1/1 at 0 Ma)",
        "does_not_claim: That Schnakenberg parameters were fitted to Coprinopsis biochemistry",
        "does_not_claim: That the growth GIF is a photograph of the fruiting body",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Explicit Euler and a periodic 5-point Laplacian",
        "reconstructed_in_script: γ calibrated so λ_c = 7.744e-05 m on a 96² grid with 12 px per wave",
        "reported_in_source: Kües 2000 developmental account of the gilled Coprinus cinereus fruiting body",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v",
        "reported_in_source: Stajich et al. 2010 Coprinopsis cinerea genome",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber from linear stability of a two-species reaction-diffusion system",
        "transfer_boundary: 77 µm is the assigned atlas scale, not a spacing measured on the photograph",
        "transfer_boundary: The photograph has no scale bar; mature gills are not the cellular wavelength" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Coprinopsis cinerea" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Slime Molds & Bacteria" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Coprinopsis" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-coprinopsis-cinerea-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/coprinopsis_cinerea_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Coprinopsis cinerea; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber from linear stability of a two-species reaction-diffusion system | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v | Kües 2000 developmental account of the gilled Coprinus cinereus fruiting body | Stajich et al. 2010 Coprinopsis cinerea genome; reconstructed_in_script: γ calibrated so λ_c = 7.744e-05 m on a 96² grid with 12 px per wave | Explicit Euler and a periodic 5-point Laplacian; transfer_boundary: 77 µm is the assigned atlas scale, not a spacing measured on the photograph | The photograph has no scale bar; mature gills are not the cellular wavelength; does_not_claim: That Schnakenberg parameters were fitted to Coprinopsis biochemistry | A predecessor or successor chronospecies (this series is 1/1 at 0 Ma) | That the growth GIF is a photograph of the fruiting body]; phenomenon_size: 82 µm (8.192e-05 m, log10=-4.087 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 82 µm to 13.4 cm): 82 µm:coprinopsis-cinerea-bioelectric-polarity, 158 µm:coprinopsis-cinerea-vertex-packing, 3.0 mm:coprinopsis-cinerea-turing-wavelength, 5.5 mm:coprinopsis-cinerea-clock-wavefront, 1.3 cm:coprinopsis-cinerea-elastic-buckling, 1.7 cm:coprinopsis-cinerea-morphogen-condensation, 2.3 cm:coprinopsis-cinerea-flux-canalization, 3.0 cm:coprinopsis-cinerea-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1003391107>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1128/MMBR.64.2.316-353.2000> ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coprinopsis-cinerea-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-coprinopsis-cinerea-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
